  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1214 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nThe renewed large scale ascent will persist from late Saturday \nafternoon through early Sunday morning. These renewed chances of \nprecipitation will favor areas off the caprock and in the extreme \nsouthern Texas Panhandle mainly after 00Z. This next short wave will \nbe much slower to exit the area keeping light rain chances going \nthrough at least Sunday afternoon. The secondary activity will see \nslightly increased chances of thunder activity as lapse rates \nsteepen with the approach of this next short wave. At the same time \non Sunday, a 1032mb surface ridge centered over the Midwest will \nsend a weak cold front through early in the day. Northeasterly \nupslope flow will again keep temperatures well below seasonal \naverages. Short wave ridging will move overhead for Monday and \nTuesday. Surface winds will veer back to the south with another \nshort wave trough moving across the western CONUS causing surface \ntroughing in lee of the Rockies. Cloud cover will likely keep \ntemperatures well below seasonal averages through Tuesday. The next \nshort wave trough around Wednesday or Thursday has become fairly \nweak in the latest model runs with little to no precipitation \nchances. Models then significantly diverge late week leading to a \nlow confidence forecast.",
